# THE BRIDE — Blud's death knight. A pale, waifish swordswoman in lace and
# plate who stalks the player and cleaves. Spec:
# docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-24-bride-sword-enemy-design.md.
#
# AUTHORED FROM PROSE plus one inspiration photo the owner showed and which is
# NOT committed (a pale slim young woman, long dark centre-parted hair, raw
# red-rimmed eyes, a white lace veil, a white corset, a short tiered ruffle
# skirt, cream thigh boots, chains and iron crosses, plate arms, a longsword
# held two-handed over the shoulder). The photo was read once for the brief
# and put down: no mesh, no plate, so blob:measure / blob:rings exit 2 and no
# number below is measured — each is a design decision with its reason beside
# it, the broodmother's road.
#
# WHO SHE IS. The broodmother's brief, turned from lust to devotion: built to
# be looked at, and WRONG BY THE SECOND LOOK. At arena distance she must read
# as graceful and female — a tall pale figure in white. Every hook below is
# something that only arrives as she closes, and none of them is allowed to
# spoil the first read.
#
# THE FOUR HOOKS, and the prims that carry each (this pass is FLESH ONLY;
# later tasks lay cloth, kit, sword and face sheet over these):
#   1. WRONG ANATOMY, THE CHEAP VERSION — the SKELETON carries it, not a prim:
#      the hip joint at 1.04 m (57% of her 1.815 m flesh height; a woman is
#      ~50%), stick-thin thighs (bar semi 0.055 at the root, 0.045 probed at
#      mid-thigh), a wasp waist (probed semi 0.087) between flared hips
#      (probed 0.169 — carried by the THIGH prims, see LEGS) and a small high
#      chest, and a 0.14 m neck (~20% too long). bride-blob.test.ts pins
#      every one of these. The SWORD FOREARM is 4 cm longer than the off one (`lenR=` on
#      `forearm`): the vambrace hides it at rest, and the swing arcs spend it
#      as a whip-like reach. No second elbow — motion joints are a fixed set.
#   2. THE VEIL HIDES A WRONG FACE — the head prims: large recessed sockets,
#      high chamfered cheekbones, a fine nose, pale
#      lips and a narrow jaw ending in a pointed chin. Pretty in its parts.
#      The WRONG half is the baked sheet (Task 2: corpse makeup, sutures from
#      the mouth corners) and the jaw gape (a later task). The eyes are dark
#      and wet, NOT glowing — she is a corpse, not a demon.
#   3. STIGMATA / RELIQUARY — the RIB WINDOW: eight thin rib ridges, four each
#      side of a sternum gap, y 1.25-1.40 on the chest bone, which the corset
#      bodice (Task 3) is clipped open over. Plus PAINTED wounds — a small
#      cross at the throat and one on each inner thigh, each with a weeping
#      drip line, in a darker, wetter red than any other paint on her.
#   4. FUSED GAUNTLETS — raw-red flesh BULGES where the plate (Task 4) will
#      meet skin: in both elbow creases and two swellings under the right
#      pauldron's rim; and a flesh CUFF on the right hand that grows past the
#      fist along the grip axis — she cannot let go of the sword.
#
# Blue-porcelain skin with a bruise-violet mottle (the palette); raw red
# 8a2a2a only at the seams; the stigmata 4a0e12, wet.
model bride
  # Flesh crown ~1.81; the scalp mass, hair and veil (Task 3) take her to
  # the spec's ~1.85.
  height 1.85
  stance humanoid

skeleton
  # THE HIGH PELVIS (hook 1). Root at 0.96 with a short 0.08 bone puts the
  # hip joint — thigh.l.head — at 1.04 m: 0.57 of her 1.815 m flesh height,
  # against ~0.50 for an ordinary woman. That is the ~10% too-long legs, and
  # it is the one proportion that reads from across the arena as "elegant"
  # before it reads as "wrong".
  root pelvis at 0.96 len=0.08

  # Upright and a little proud: the lumbar sways back 2, the chest lifts
  # (pitch -3). She carries herself; the zombie owns the stoop.
  bone spine1 parent=pelvis dir=up pitch=-2 len=0.15
  bone chest  parent=spine1 dir=up pitch=-3 len=0.17
  bone spine2 parent=chest  dir=up pitch=0  len=0.07
  # THE LONG NECK (hook 1): 0.14 m, ~20% over the ~0.115 a woman of her
  # height carries, pitched 8 forward so the head floats ahead of the
  # shoulders like a swan's — graceful first, stalk-like on the second look.
  bone neck   parent=spine2 dir=up pitch=8  len=0.14
  # Skull tipped back 4 so the face lifts: the chin leads. The face features
  # below hang off this bone at=0.08..0.62 (y 1.59..1.72).
  bone skull  parent=neck   dir=up pitch=-4 len=0.24

  mirror
    # NARROW, SLOPING SHOULDERS: socket at x ~0.15, y ~1.41 — a slight
    # woman's frame (the deltoid's outer surface lands ~0.19). tilt -8 drops
    # the socket below the yoke's top: at tilt 4 the deltoids rose 2 cm over
    # the shoulder line and read as a mannequin's ball joints. (On a `side`
    # bone tilt swings toward +y, so negative is down.) The WAM pauldron
    # (Task 4) widens the right one.
    bone clavicle parent=spine2   side=0.020 dir=side tilt=-8 len=0.13
    # Arms long and thin, hanging out (tilt 11, forearm 6) so there is
    # DAYLIGHT between wrist and hip flare (semi ~0.16): at tilt 8 / 4 the
    # probed flesh ran unbroken from the navel to the forearm at y 1.00.
    # Forward a touch (pitch 2).
    bone upperarm parent=clavicle dir=down tilt=11 pitch=2 len=0.30
    # THE SWORD FOREARM (hook 1): 0.26 on the off side, 0.30 on the sword
    # side. lenR= is the grammar's asymmetric-pair word (added for her): a
    # mirror block otherwise gives both sides one length, and a bone outside
    # it could neither parent to upperarm.r nor carry arm prims. The right
    # hand hangs 4 cm lower at rest; the vambrace hides where.
    bone forearm  parent=upperarm dir=down tilt=6 pitch=10 len=0.26 lenR=0.30
    bone hand     parent=forearm  dir=down pitch=8         len=0.08
    # LEGS: 0.49 + 0.48 from the hip joint at 1.04 lands the ankle at ~0.07.
    # Knees drawn in a whisper (tilt -1.5, shins +1.5) — a narrow, poised
    # stance with a daylight gap between stick-thin thighs. Knee a touch
    # FORWARD of the hip-ankle line (thigh pitch 2, shin -1): a first pass
    # with the shin pitched +1 folded the knee 4 mm BEHIND it, which
    # checkStance reads as digitigrade and the lab refuses to load.
    bone thigh    parent=pelvis dir=down tilt=-1.5 pitch=2 side=0.085 len=0.49
    bone shin     parent=thigh  dir=down tilt=1.5  pitch=-1 len=0.48
    # The foot bone only positions the foot prims (the house pattern).
    bone foot     parent=shin   dir=fwd                      len=0.13
  end

body
  # ============================================================
  # TORSO — the hourglass (hook 1). Waist 0.087, ribcage 0.115 (hips: see LEGS),
  # every mass a tapered bar with heavy overlap so it reads as one smooth
  # body, not stacked discs (the schoolgirl lesson).
  # BLENDS ARE ~1.4-2x the first pass on every round union: buildBody
  # halves them (roundBlendScale 0.5), and the first frames read as a
  # jointed wooden mannequin — a knob at every shoulder, a "diaper" of hip
  # under a stick waist, rings at the knees. A straight 2x overshot: the
  # smooth-min's added volume took the probed waist from 0.089 to 0.131
  # and fused the elbows to the hips.
  # ============================================================
  # Pelvis: the bowl the thighs root in. Semi-width 0.126, bottom at
  # y ~0.89 — kept SMALL. The hip flare is NOT here (see LEGS): the first
  # three passes built it as torso blobs and every one read as a light bulb
  # (a "diaper") hung over two sticks, because torso and leg are different
  # clusters and meet with a hard seam, so no blend can carry the outer
  # line from hip into thigh.
  blob torso on pelvis at=0.35 r=0.105 wide=1.20 tall=0.90 deep=0.84 blend=0.028
  # WASP WAIST: one tapered bar up spine1 (y 1.04 -> 1.19). Probed semi-
  # width at its narrowest (y 1.13) is the number the spec caps at 0.095;
  # r 0.080/0.074 x 1.20 probed 0.095 — on the cap, not under it — so the
  # bar is pulled in (and the ribcage's root with it): now 0.087. Shallow
  # deep so the belly is flat.
  bar  torso on spine1 from=0.00 to=1.00 r=0.072 r2=0.058 wide=1.16 deep=0.80 blend=0.026
  # RIBCAGE: flares from the waist to 0.115 semi at the top of the chest
  # bone (y 1.36). This is the surface the rib ridges lie on. `core`: the
  # structural mass the arms, neck and hips all fuse to.
  bar  torso on chest  from=0.00 to=0.88 r=0.072 r2=0.098 wide=1.17 deep=0.84 blend=0.024 core
  # Small, HIGH chest: two low mounds at y ~1.35, set wide (x 0.068) so the
  # sternum strip between them — the rib window — stays open.
  blob torso on chest  at=0.95 offset=(0.068,-0.018,0.052) r=0.036 deep=0.95 blend=0.022 both
  # THE RIB WINDOW (hook 3). Four ribs each side of a 3 cm sternum gap,
  # sternal ends at y 1.385 / 1.350 / 1.315 / 1.280, each running out to
  # x ~0.08 and dropping 2.7-3.5 cm as real ribs do (steeper lower down).
  # Task 3 clips the bodice open over exactly this strip. Every endpoint's z
  # is the PROBED front surface of the chest there (sdBody, scratch probe)
  # minus ~1.5 mm, so an r 0.0055 ridge stands ~4 mm proud: ribs pressing
  # against skin, not bones laid on it. bend= is the probed surface bulge at
  # each rib's midpoint over its chord. Unpainted: shading carries them.
  # The chest bone's at=0.50 is (0, 1.275, -0.0095); offsets are from there.
  bar  torso on chest from=0.50 to=0.50 offset=(0.016,0.110,0.0725) tip=(0.066,-0.027,0.0025) bend=(0,0,0.0012) r=0.0055 blend=0.004 both
  bar  torso on chest from=0.50 to=0.50 offset=(0.016,0.075,0.0780) tip=(0.066,-0.028,0) bend=(0,0,0.0065) r=0.0055 blend=0.004 both
  bar  torso on chest from=0.50 to=0.50 offset=(0.016,0.040,0.0765) tip=(0.066,-0.030,-0.025) bend=(0,0,0.012) r=0.0055 blend=0.004 both
  bar  torso on chest from=0.50 to=0.50 offset=(0.016,0.005,0.0710) tip=(0.064,-0.035,-0.036) bend=(0,0,0.0085) r=0.0055 blend=0.004 both
  # Yoke + shoulder line: thin front-to-back, semi-width 0.135 — a narrow
  # woman's shoulders sloping into the long neck.
  blob torso on spine2 at=0.90 r=0.060 wide=2.35 tall=0.62 deep=0.85 blend=0.030

  # ============================================================
  # HEAD + NECK (hook 2). The face block is a NUB; every feature is a prim
  # (broodmother's road). Skull bone runs (0,1.568,0.005) -> (0,1.808,-0.011);
  # the cranium's front is z ~0.095 at the eye line, ~0.077 at the mouth.
  # Every feature's z below is set against THOSE numbers (a first pass
  # used z 0.020 for the skull root and buried half the face 1.5 cm deep).
  # ============================================================
  # THE NECK: long — elegance is length — and slim at the top (0.034), but
  # flaring to 0.043 at the base so it grows out of the shoulders: at a
  # constant 0.034 it read as a stalk on a mannequin.
  bar  head on neck from=0.00 to=1.00 r=0.043 r2=0.034 deep=1.05 blend=0.028
  # HEAD BLENDS ARE SMALL ON PURPOSE. Smooth-min swell ACCUMULATES: where
  # the cranium, the lower-face cone, the jaw angle and a cheekbone are all
  # ~2 cm away, four blends of 0.02-0.03 folded the field 1.9 cm negative
  # (sdBody -0.003 at a point every prim called +0.016), and the head grew
  # a band 0.092 wide at eye level — goggles, with a moustache of shadow
  # under them. The worst offender was CHAMFER: its reach is 4 x blend and
  # buildBody does NOT halve it (only round unions), so the cheekbones'
  # chamfer 0.008 bevelled 3.2 cm of air into flesh. Chamfers here are
  # 0.002-0.003; round head blends 0.010-0.014.
  # CRANIUM: narrow and a little long, centre y ~1.708, semi (0.076, 0.108,
  # 0.100). The fattest head prim: the frame the Task 2 sheet projects from.
  blob head on skull at=0.58 r=0.098 wide=0.78 tall=1.10 deep=1.02 blend=0.010
  # THE LOWER FACE is ONE tapered cone from under the cheeks (y 1.664,
  # r 0.050, front z 0.0965 — 4.5 mm INSIDE the cranium's front there, so it
  # never bulges past it) down to the chin (y 1.594, r 0.024): a V that
  # narrows to the chin with no seam across it. Two earlier passes put a
  # mass proud of the cranium (a jaw ellipsoid, then this cone rooted at eye
  # height) and the ledge under it shaded, below the nose, as a handlebar
  # MOUSTACHE. Mouth-height (y 1.635) front z ~0.090.
  blob head on skull at=0.40 offset=(0,0,0.036) tip=(0,-0.070,0.022) r=0.050 r2=0.024 wide=1.25 blend=0.012
  # Jaw angle: the mass behind the V that gives the jaw line its width,
  # set back (front z ~0.07) so it never reaches the face plane.
  blob head on skull at=0.22 offset=(0,-0.005,0.000) r=0.055 wide=1.05 tall=0.90 deep=1.00 blend=0.014
  # POINTED CHIN: a short chamfered taper forward and down, bottom y ~1.585.
  blob head on skull at=0.08 offset=(0,0.002,0.052) tip=(0,-0.012,0.014) r=0.022 r2=0.009 blend=0.003 chamfer
  # HIGH CHEEKBONES, chamfered so they keep an edge under the sockets; the
  # hollow below them is what the sheet's contour paint deepens later. HIGH
  # means just under the eye and out toward the temple (y ~1.683, x 0.048):
  # the first pass sat them beside the nose (y 1.667, x 0.040) and they
  # puffed out as a chipmunk's cheeks.
  blob head on skull at=0.50 offset=(0.046,-0.012,0.060) r=0.014 wide=1.25 tall=0.60 deep=0.90 blend=0.003 chamfer both
  # LARGE SOCKETS: bruised ovals set near-flush (front ~4 mm proud of the
  # cranium at x 0.029) — big dark eyes are the "pretty" read at range.
  # Taller than wide-ish (tall 1.05): at 1.30 x 0.90, pinched by brow and
  # cheek, they read as black slits — sunglasses, not eyes. Bruise red-
  # violet (5a2530), a step lighter than the eye, so the eyeball reads
  # inside it; the Task 2 sheet adds the smoky makeup.
  blob head on skull at=0.55 offset=(0.029,0,0.075) r=0.020 wide=1.15 tall=1.05 blend=0.004 both color=5a2530
  # EYES: dark and wet, NOT glowing. ~6 mm proud of the socket.
  blob head on skull at=0.55 offset=(0.029,-0.001,0.087) r=0.012 blend=0.002 both color=120a0c gloss=0.90
  # FINE NOSE: a chamfered ridge from just below the eye line down and out
  # (rooted at the eye line it stood between the sockets as a lump),
  # r 0.0065 -> 0.0045 (0.008 -> 0.006 read as a potato from the front),
  # tip ~1.7 cm proud. The refinement the rest is measured
  # against.
  blob head on skull at=0.52 offset=(0,0.002,0.090) tip=(0,-0.036,0.017) r=0.0065 r2=0.0045 wide=0.85 blend=0.002 chamfer
  # STIGMATA, THROAT (hook 3): a small cross over the windpipe at y ~1.50
  # (neck at=0.45 is (0, 1.492, -0.006); front surface z ~0.035) and one
  # thin drip weeping down to the notch. The darkest, wettest paint on her:
  # 4a0e12 at gloss 0.85: a 3.2 x 2.0 cm cross of 1.8 mm bars. At 4.4 x
  # 2.8 cm / 2.4 mm the arms and drip merged into one 2.5 cm red teardrop
  # in the 0.5 m close-up — a wound you see, not a mark you find — a mark you find, not a wound you see.
  blob head on neck at=0.45 offset=(0,0.016,0.040) tip=(0,-0.032,0.001) r=0.0018 blend=0.001 color=4a0e12 gloss=0.85
  blob head on neck at=0.45 offset=(-0.010,0.006,0.040) tip=(0.020,0,0) bend=(0,0,0.003) r=0.0018 blend=0.001 color=4a0e12 gloss=0.85
  blob head on neck at=0.45 offset=(0.001,-0.016,0.039) tip=(0.002,-0.040,-0.006) r=0.0016 r2=0.0008 blend=0.001 color=4a0e12 gloss=0.85
  # PALE LIPS: two bent bars bowed over the jaw's curve, grey-lilac — the
  # corpse makeup's mouth, before the sheet adds the sutures.
  # 3.0 cm / 2.6 cm across, thin upper, fuller lower, each ~half PROUD of
  # the face (front z ~0.090). Paint goes to the hit's nearest prim
  # (prim-material.wgsl hitBest), and round the lips that claims more of
  # the face than the lips themselves: the colour paints a ~4 cm patch. So
  # the tint is kept a step off the skin (b8a4b0), pale, not pink.
  bar  head on skull from=0.30 to=0.30 offset=(-0.015,0,0.079) tip=(0.030,0,0) bend=(0,0.001,0.006) r=0.0040 tall=0.90 blend=0.003 color=b8a4b0 gloss=0.45
  bar  head on skull from=0.30 to=0.30 offset=(-0.013,-0.009,0.078) tip=(0.026,0,0) bend=(0,-0.002,0.007) r=0.0052 tall=0.85 blend=0.003 color=b8a4b0 gloss=0.45

  # ============================================================
  # ARMS. Under plate from shoulder to fingertip (Task 4), so the flesh is
  # thin and plain — except at the SEAMS (hook 4).
  # ============================================================
  blob arm on upperarm at=0.00 r=0.037 blend=0.024 mirror core
  bar  arm on upperarm from=0.04 to=0.97 r=0.036 r2=0.028 blend=0.016 mirror
  bar  arm on forearm  from=0.02 to=0.96 r=0.029 r2=0.021 blend=0.014 mirror
  blob arm on hand     at=0.45 r=0.024 wide=0.75 tall=1.20 deep=1.15 blend=0.016 mirror
  # FUSED SEAMS (hook 4), raw red 8a2a2a where the plate will meet skin.
  # ELBOW CREASE: the couter covers the point of the elbow; the forearm is
  # pitched forward, so the crease faces +z, and the flesh swells ~1.7 cm
  # out of that gap. Both arms.
  blob arm on upperarm at=1.00 offset=(0,0.004,0.027) r=0.018 wide=1.05 tall=0.80 blend=0.010 mirror color=8a2a2a gloss=0.55
  # UNDER THE PAULDRON (sword side only): two swellings bulging out below
  # where the pauldron's rim will sit (~upperarm 0.25-0.30, y ~1.35),
  # outboard and front/back. side=r offsets are NOT mirrored: -x is out.
  blob arm on upperarm at=0.30 offset=(-0.030,0,0.012) r=0.020 blend=0.010 side=r color=8a2a2a gloss=0.55
  blob arm on upperarm at=0.24 offset=(-0.022,0,-0.026) r=0.018 blend=0.010 side=r color=8a2a2a gloss=0.55
  # THE CUFF (hook 4): flesh that has grown over the sword hand and on past
  # the fist along the grip axis (the carry's elbow->hand line, carry.ts
  # gunPoseFromArm), tapering to a tendril ~5 cm beyond the hand bone's tail
  # — into the hilt. Fatter than the mitt so it reads OVER the gauntlet
  # (Task 4 sizes the gauntlet under it). A raw ring where it roots at the
  # wrist.
  blob arm on forearm at=0.97 r=0.026 wide=1.10 tall=0.60 blend=0.008 side=r color=8a2a2a gloss=0.55
  blob arm on hand at=0.10 tip=(0,-0.125,0.018) r=0.031 r2=0.016 blend=0.010 side=r

  # ============================================================
  # LEGS. Stick-thin (hook 1): thigh semi 0.055 at the root tapering to 0.036
  # at the knee, a small hard calf, narrow feet. The cream boots (Task 4)
  # cover them from the thigh down.
  # ============================================================
  # HIP FLARE — on the THIGH, where anatomy puts the widest point of the
  # hips (the greater trochanter is femur): a mass out and a little back of
  # the hip joint, outer surface x ~0.165 at y ~1.00 (probed), flowing in one smooth
  # leg-cluster blend down the outside of the thigh. It swings with the leg,
  # which is right. The bottom of the hourglass (hook 1).
  blob leg on thigh at=0.09 offset=(0.014,0,-0.010) r=0.060 tall=1.30 deep=1.00 blend=0.030 mirror core
  bar  leg on thigh from=0.04 to=1.00 r=0.055 r2=0.036 deep=1.05 blend=0.020 mirror
  # Bars run to the joint and overlap: stopped short (0.97 / 0.03) with a
  # knee ball between, the knee read as a doll's ring joint.
  bar  leg on shin  from=0.00 to=0.97 r=0.037 r2=0.022 blend=0.020 mirror
  # STIGMATA, INNER THIGHS (hook 3): a cross on the inner-front of each
  # thigh at y ~0.93 (thigh at=0.22, flesh r ~0.055 with the root's blend; the cross sits 30
  # degrees round from the inside toward the front, so it shows between the
  # thighs from the front), and a drip weeping 10 cm down toward where the
  # stockings (Task 3) will start. Offsets are for .l (+x out); mirror
  # reflects them for .r. The horizontal arm runs along the surface tangent.
  blob leg on thigh at=0.22 offset=(-0.048,0.016,0.029) tip=(0.001,-0.032,0) r=0.0030 blend=0.002 mirror color=4a0e12 gloss=0.85
  blob leg on thigh at=0.22 offset=(-0.0540,0.005,0.0190) tip=(0.0114,0,0.0187) r=0.0030 blend=0.002 mirror color=4a0e12 gloss=0.85
  blob leg on thigh at=0.22 offset=(-0.048,-0.016,0.029) tip=(0.002,-0.100,-0.002) r=0.0024 r2=0.0012 blend=0.002 mirror color=4a0e12 gloss=0.85
  # Calf: a small high swell at the back — muscle on a starved frame.
  blob leg on shin  at=0.26 offset=(0,0,-0.010) r=0.034 deep=1.15 blend=0.024 mirror
  # Foot: one tapered bar, sole at y ~0.01, arch-high heel end.
  bar  leg on foot  from=0.00 to=0.90 offset=(0,-0.036,-0.010) r=0.030 r2=0.021 wide=1.10 tall=0.80 blend=0.018 mirror

# Wound pass: hidden bone. Torso and skull are AUTHORED — partly for the
# budget (auto-derive would grow a bone in every rib ridge, bust mound and
# face feature) and partly because a headshot and a chest shot are the
# shots players take. Limbs auto-derive (ratio 0.38).
bones
  ratio 0.38
  # Cranium: ~1.6-2 cm of flesh on every side of the (0.076,0.108,0.100) head.
  blob head on skull at=0.58 r=0.078 wide=0.78 tall=1.08 deep=1.00
  # Spine through the waist, a ribcage, a pelvic bowl.
  bar  torso on spine1 from=0.00 to=1.00 r=0.024
  blob torso on chest  at=0.55 r=0.062 wide=1.25 tall=1.25 deep=0.85
  blob torso on pelvis at=0.30 r=0.080 wide=1.25 tall=0.80 deep=0.85

# No mesh, so no bake yet: every face feature is a prim above and the face
# block is a NUB so the parameterised ellipsoid cannot fight the cranium.
face
  headRadius 0.001
  headWidth  1.0
  headHeight 1.0
  headDepth  1.0
  jawWidth   1.0
  jawHeight  1.0
  jawDrop    0
  jawJut     0
  noseLength 0
  noseWidth  1.0
  noseDrop   0
  browHeavy  0
  browRise   0
  headBlend  0.006

# The generated sheet is OFF until the baked corpse-makeup sheet (Task 2).
# With no sheet block the lab multiplies the shared default sheet over the
# head, and on a prim face it paints greasepaint round the eyes (broodmother).
sheet
  enabled 0

# BLUE PORCELAIN: a cold, slightly blue pale (linear 0.62 0.64 0.70) — not
# the schoolgirl's warm skin, not the zombie's grey-green: a body kept too
# long in a cold chapel. A bruise-VIOLET mottle (a hue shift, not a darker
# base, or it vanishes — broodmother). Translucent enough to glow a little at
# the rim, a faint wet sheen: beautiful first.
palette
  baseColor     0.62 0.64 0.70
  deepColor     0.50 0.05 0.08
  charColor     0.07 0.05 0.06
  specIntensity 0.45
  specRoughness 0.38
  fresnelBoost  0.35
  translucency  0.25
  wetness       0.20
  surfaceNoiseAmp    0.015
  silhouetteNoiseAmp 0.004
  mottleAmp     0.30
  mottleScale   2.2
  mottleColor   0.36 0.26 0.42
